    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `build_client` in `app/llm_client.py` and all tests pass (3 passed).\n\n**Watch out:** openai 3.19.2 builds on **`httpx2`**, not `httpx`. Plain `httpx` isn't installed in the venv. The code imports `httpx2`, and the `transport` passed in must be an `httpx2` transport such as `httpx2.MockTransport`. An `httpx.MockTransport` won't work, so check any stubs written against `httpx`.\n\nHow each requirement is met:\n1. **Timeouts:** `httpx2.Timeout(30.0, connect=5.0)`, so connect is 5s and read, write and pool are 30s. It's set on both the `OpenAI` client and the HTTP client. The SDK sends its own timeout with every request, so setting it on the HTTP client alone wouldn't be reliable.\n2. **Retries:** `max_retries=2` is passed to `OpenAI`.\n3. **Logging:** a `\"request\"` event hook logs `\"<METHOD> <URL>\"` at INFO on the `app.http` logger. The SDK's retry loop sends each attempt through the HTTP client, so retries are logged too.\n4. **Transport:** it's passed to the HTTP client when given; with `None`, the default network transport is used. The HTTP client is built with openai's `DefaultHttpxClient`, so it keeps the SDK's defaults for connection limits and redirect-following.\n\nI added `tests/test_llm_client.py` with two tests:\n- One checks the timeouts and `max_retries`.\n- One sends requests to a mock transport that always returns 500. It checks that the three attempts (the first plus two retries) each produce one INFO log line: `GET https://api.openai.com/v1/models`. It sets the delay between retries to zero so the test runs quickly.\n\nNo dependencies were added or changed."
